Ubiquiti Cloud Gateway Fiber (UCG-Fiber) Configuration
Companion configuration to the Catalyst 2960-X (OOB) and Nexus 9000 (core) switches. The UCG Fiber terminates trunks from both switches and performs all inter-VLAN routing and firewall policy — neither switch does L3 routing.

The UCG Fiber does not use an IOS-style CLI config file. Everything below is configured through the UniFi Network application (GUI/API), with an optional config.gateway.json override for anything not exposed in the UI.

Important: VLAN 40 renumbering
On the switches, trunk VLAN IDs are only locally significant per link, so VLAN 40 could safely mean different things on the 2960-X (INFRA_TAILSCALE) and the Nexus (INFRA_SERVICES). On the gateway this breaks: UniFi's "Networks" are defined once globally, keyed by VLAN ID, and applied to ports/SSIDs. Since the UCG Fiber terminates both switches, the Nexus's VLAN 40 was renumbered to VLAN 41 (INFRA_SERVICES) to avoid the collision. Apply that renumbering to the Nexus switch config before wiring it to this gateway.

