Port Profiles (Settings → Networks → Port Profiles)
Apply these to whichever physical ports are cabled to each switch. Verify actual port labels against your specific UCG-Fiber hardware/firmware revision before assigning — SFP+/SFP28/RJ45 layout varies.

Profile: TRUNK-TO-2960X-OOB

Native Network: BLACKHOLE_NATIVE (or "None")
Tagged VLANs: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80
Profile: TRUNK-TO-NEXUS-CORE

Native Network: BLACKHOLE_NATIVE (or "None")
Tagged VLANs: 20, 30, 31, 41, 100
Traffic/Firewall Rules (Settings → Security → Traffic Rules / Firewall Rules)
Implements the isolation intent documented in both switch configs:

VLAN 21 (Corosync): no rules needed — it is not trunked to this gateway and has no gateway address. Isolation is structural (L2-only on the Nexus).
Block VLAN 31 (PBS Backup) → Internet; restrict to PBS↔PVE traffic only.
Block Tailscale-sourced traffic → VLAN 31 explicitly (enforces "do not route PBS backup through Tailscale" — don't rely on omission). VLAN 21 is unreachable from here by design (no SVI, no trunk).
VLAN 50 (IoT) → deny to VLANs 10, 20, 30, 80; allow IoT → Internet only.
VLAN 80 (AP mgmt) → allow only from an admin/management source; deny from IoT/Apple TV/iPhones.
Default posture: inter-VLAN deny, with explicit allows layered on top.
mDNS/AirPlay (Settings → Networks → VLAN 60/70 → Multicast DNS)
Enable Multicast DNS (mDNS) on both the Apple TV (60) and iPhones (70) networks. This lets iPhones on VLAN 70 discover the Apple TV on VLAN 60 via UniFi's built-in mDNS reflector, without merging the two VLANs.

Advanced: config.gateway.json
Anything above not exposed in the UI (fine-grained per-VLAN routing policy, static routes) can be layered in via the JSON config override under UniFi OS. Hold off writing this until the GUI configuration above is in place and tested — firmware-schema details vary by UniFi OS version, and a bad override can lock you out of the gateway.

